# uml2semantics (Python)

CLI/library to convert UML-style TSV specifications into an OWL 2 ontology using rdflib.

Supported inputs:
- Classes.tsv
- Attributes.tsv
- Enumerations.tsv
- EnumerationNamedValues.tsv
- Datatypes.tsv
- AnnotationProperties.tsv (new)
- Annotations.tsv (new)

## New in v0.6.0

- Added TSV-driven **annotation properties**:
  - `AnnotationProperties.tsv` to declare annotation properties.
  - `Annotations.tsv` to attach annotations to Ontology, Class, Property, Datatype, Enumeration, or Individual.
- Extended multiplicity handling:
  - When `MinMultiplicity` and `MaxMultiplicity` are both numeric and equal (`n..n`), the generator emits a single `owl:cardinality n` restriction.
  - Otherwise, retains the `someValuesFrom` + `maxCardinality` pattern.
- Extended examples:
  - ISO 4217 `CurrencyCode` enumeration.
  - Named datatypes: `ISO4217CurrencyCode`, `LEI20`, `BIC11` with regex + length facets.
  - A simple LEI/BIC choice structure for trade party identification.

## Quickstart

```bash
pip install .

uml2semantics   -c examples/Classes.tsv   -a examples/Attributes.tsv   --datatypes examples/Datatypes.tsv   -e examples/Enumerations.tsv   -n examples/EnumerationNamedValues.tsv   --annotation-properties examples/AnnotationProperties.tsv   --annotations examples/Annotations.tsv   -o out.owl   -p "iso:http://iso20022.example/ontology#,rdfs:http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#,skos:http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#"   -i "http://iso20022.example/ontology"
```
